WEBVTT

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.860
At any rate, I'm going to look for Hayate.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.360
And then... I'll try talking to him again.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.370
Will you...

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.740
...help me find him?

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.710
Of course!

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.430
Hey. We'll help you find him, too.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.470
Everyone...

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.220
It's not your fault that 
Hayate-kun's gone, Nagi.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.100
Huh?

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.450
He made no prior indication that
 he disliked being a butler.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.250
Right.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.020
I'm sure he left because a dumb friend

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.610
did something stupid.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.170
Shoot, where is this dumb friend?

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.610
We won't forgive them!

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.370
What?

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.160
It's our fault?

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.190
Yup.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.710
No, you're mistaken!

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.140
We'd never do anything 
to bother Hayata-kun.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.580
Well, actually, we always do...

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.550
But not something so big that 
he disappears in America.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.750
Putting the jokes aside...

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.800
Where should we start looking?

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.080
Hayate-kun's cell phone isn't working,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.640
so we can't get in touch with him.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.540
That's a problem.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:30.470
Doesn't that thing bring bad luck?

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:32.830
Yeah.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:37.730
Why don't you put it 
in a safe or something?

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.180
I could.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.290
Why does Tsugumi want that clock?

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.820
I know it brings the owner bad luck,

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.870
but when both hands strike eight,

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.230
incredibly good luck comes your way.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.660
Yeah? Is that right?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.640
But would she want such a 
creepy clock just for that?

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.580
Did you see that woman's reaction 
when we said it was lost?

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.350
She was furious.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.820
Like her parents or lover 
was killed, or something.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:13.940
What's wrong?

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.700
It's just... I...

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:20.450
Maybe...

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.550
I've misunderstood everything.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.380
<i>Goodbye, Miss Nagi.</i>

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.600
Now that I think about it, 
all these weird things have happened.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.720
That anger...

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.730
And my father, who betrayed my 
mother and died 13 years ago.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.480
<i>The black camellia is a magical sword.</i>

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:17.800
<i>The king's sword,</i>

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.320
<i>which grants eternity 
to anyone stabbed by it.</i>

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.110
Magical, huh?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:27.290
You also do things that 
bother Hayata-kun, Izumi.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.790
What? No way.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.180
You're lying!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.310
You said Hayata-kun was stabbed

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.930
yesterday trying to help you.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.170
B-But...

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.050
W-Wait. What do you mean, stabbed?

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.290
Um, he wasn't hurt or anything, but...

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.560
The thief who had the black camellia

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:54.940
pulled a black sword out of 
nowhere, and then... Stab!

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.440
It looked like he'd stabbed 
Hayata-kun, but...

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.160
You saw it too, right, Hina-chan?

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.320
Yes, I was shocked.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.410
A black sword.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.870
<i>The black camellia really is a clock...</i>

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.450
<i>I'd heard of a sword with the same name.</i>

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:18.170
Are you saying the clock transformed 
into the shape of a sword?

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.420
Um... Yeah, it looked like it might have.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.560
<i>What if the black camellia really is a</i>

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.660
<i>magical sword that possesses 
mysterious powers?</i>

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.250
<i>The man who betrayed Yukariko</i>

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.120
<i>and stole the black camellia...</i>

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.230
<i>...was your father, Shin Hayek.</i>

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.840
<i>But Shin-chan was a bit careless, too.</i>

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.060
<i>And also...</i>

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.330
<i>Do you have proof your 
father had an affair?</i>

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.190
<i>Well, maybe.</i>

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.080
<i>Hey... Is it true?</i>

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.200
<i>Even as he was dying, he asked me, 
"How can you say that?"</i>

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.460
<i>What did he say?</i>

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.000
<i>Well...</i>

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:09.510
<i>No. No. It can't be! There's no way!</i>

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:14.180
<i>But if it is true...</i>

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.850
<i>The pieces fit together.</i>

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.360
<i>It's hard to believe, 
but I need to check.</i>

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.330
<i>If my guess is right...</i>

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.720
<i>Then the black camellia is...</i>

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.340
Tsugumi!

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.080
I finally got the black camellia!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.570
Stop, Tsugumi!

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:44.090
Do you realize what that is?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.550
I know.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.550
It's a clock that brings bad luck.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.930
Well, that's technically true.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.650
But that's not all.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:05.650
I finally see what that monster's after.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:10.260
It seems inconceivable, 
so I can't say for sure, but...

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.390
Tsugumi.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.180
Wh-What?

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:17.370
Your big sister has a favor to ask of you.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:18.870
Huh?

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.230
I want you to get me the ring that's

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:25.750
on the right hand of the 
woman you call your mother.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.670
What? You think it's that easy?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.950
She only takes the ring 
off when she bathes!

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:34.380
Don't be insane!

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.390
Please.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.000
Hayate's life depends on it.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.460
So... Please.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.020
O-Oh, all right.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.400
Thanks, Tsugumi.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.480
Let me know when you get it.

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.030
I'll let you know where we'll meet.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:02.870
But you have to promise to
 give me the black camellia!

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:03.570
Sure.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:08.600
Um... Why is Hayate-kun's life in danger?

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:11.200
Sorry, I don't have time to explain.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.630
Besides, Maria...

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.640
I need something brought 
over from Japan, ASAP!

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:21.080
If it's small, we can have
 a special jet deliver it

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.350
in about three hours.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.430
Three hours?

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:24.100
Please.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:28.070
Can we get in touch with Ruka?

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:28.780
Huh?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.320
She's probably rehearsing for her show.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.120
I need her help with something.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.190
Thanks for waiting.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:17.990
This is...

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.860
My mother's wedding ring.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.550
We won't find Hayate
 by blindly searching for him.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:29.820
But they're looking for
 the same thing we are!

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:37.330
Ruka-san! Where did you get that ring?

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.480
My friend lent it to 
me for the show today.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.760
Wow! The ring she is wearing

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:49.860
seems to be worth 
over three million dollars.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.650
I can't believe it!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:57.400
We've asked the TV stations 
to keep airing the footage.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.370
Yeah, I hope this works.

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.340
<i>Wearing a ring borrowed from</i>

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.420
<i>her millionaire friend, Ruka expects</i>

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:13.960
<i>to start her concert at 
8 p.m. on the Starside Stage!</i>

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.550
That's...

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:31.400
<i>I'll prove that he doesn't love you.</i>

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.790
<i>Give him this.</i>

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:37.510
<i>Once he learns it's 
worth 200 million yen,</i>

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:41.410
<i>I'm sure he'll sell it and come up 
with an excuse, like saying he lost it.</i>

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:46.650
<i>Since he's only after money, not love.</i>

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:08.980
You tell me to go get it, 
but it isn't that easy!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.120
Wow! Here it is!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:31.930
Now I'll help my big sister 
and save Hayate Ayasaki.

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:36.930
No, no! I'll trade this 
for the black camellia.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:41.470
I-I better tell my big 
sister I have the ring.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:41.460
<b> OK</b>

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.280
D-Don't scare me like that!

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.140
Um...

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.060
...at 7 p.m. at the Starside Hotel.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.350
Hurry!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:11:59.940
To the...

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:03.410
...Starside Hotel!

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:11.410
Whoa, there's tons of people.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.660
Ruka-chan's something else.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.250
She sure is.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.730
This is quite a success!

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.260
Do you think Hayate-kun's here?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.760
I'm not sure, but Nagi said

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:24.570
not to worry and just enjoy the show.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.400
Okay, then.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.180
I thought so.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.000
Huh? What?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.450
There was something weird about

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.190
the story Sakuya told us

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.670
earlier about the black camellia.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:36.690
Something weird?

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:40.860
Yeah, the hands on a clock never

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:43.610
strike eight at the same time.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.690
Are you sure you're okay on your own?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.750
I'd like to do this alone.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:57.130
Even if I say I'll come, 
 you'll tell me no.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:58.720
Sorry.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.960
And you've been holding onto that...

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.220
But wouldn't a safe be preferable?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.180
No. I don't care what kind of 
bad luck comes my way.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:13.920
I'm never gonna let this go.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:17.930
I'm off.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:19.490
Um, Nagi?

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:20.430
What?

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:24.170
Nothing. Be careful.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.340
This is it.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.590
What, are you going to war?

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:48.010
I'm sending all the guys 
who stole my money to Hell.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.220
Try not to die.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:58.000
Time to make my move too.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.950
<b><i>May I touch the hand reaching out to me?</i></b>

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.940
<b><i>The wind blows through my fingers</i></b>

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:23.670
<b><i>as I uncertainly reach to open the door.</i></b>

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:39.680
The ring's on the top floor, in the wedding hall.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:39.680
 Nagi Sanzenin

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:39.320
Nagi.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:58.770
You're here.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:02.360
I didn't think it would happen like this.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:05.590
You don't have to speak 
to me like a butler.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:11.810
I finally understand the 
secret of the black camellia.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.700
The black camellia is a magical sword?

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:21.020
Yes, I asked my great 
grandmother about it earlier.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.960
It's a magical sword made by a king

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.360
who wished for eternal life.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:30.610
It exchanges a person's soul.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.120
E-Exchanges souls?

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.630
The black camellia

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.540
takes a soul from a body...

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.050
...and...

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.590
...exchanges it for the soul of

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.160
the next person stabbed by it.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:00.830
From an old body to a youthful one.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.360
Thus, a soul can continue being reborn

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.870
if you keep putting it into a new body.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:17.680
That monster, Dolly, must've repeated 
the process over and over

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:21.120
to grant eternity to her king.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:26.050
But Dolly made a mistake and 
lost the black camellia,

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.130
which contained the king's soul.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:31.410
The black camellia then fell into

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.510
the possession of the Sanzenin family.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.300
Since Dolly can't leave her 
sanctuary for very long,

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.600
she tricked novice thieves to try to

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.020
make them get the black camellia for her.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.520
That was 13 years ago.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.020
However, an unexpected 
miscalculation happened.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:53.030
A man who didn't know what 
the black camellia was...

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.030
...randomly touched it.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.210
And then...

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.710
He was stabbed by

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:18.510
the black camellia when 
he got into an accident.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.640
Then, 13 years went by.

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:27.860
His soul was trapped in the

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:31.320
black camellia until Hayate 
was stabbed yesterday.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:35.200
Am I right, Father?

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.360
Yukariko died?

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.720
Yes, eight years ago.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.940
Her grave's in Shimoda, 
the city of your honeymoon.

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:03.510
She said that town held 
her best memories of you.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.250
I see.

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:11.310
What did she say about me?

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:15.960
Well, she said you were careless.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:16.610
What?

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.120
And her favorite thing about you 
was that you were handsome.

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:23.870
I don't know if I should 
take that as a compliment.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:26.080
How was she supposed to compliment

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.380
a guy who let his wedding ring get stolen,

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:29.860
was manipulated by a monster,

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.260
and got into a car accident while

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.380
getting the ring back?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.860
H-How do you know all of that?

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:37.660
But she wasn't mad.

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:44.520
Mother always looked happy 
when she talked about you.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:49.880
My guess is that she loved 
everything about you, including that.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.270
I see.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.160
You okay holding onto that?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.210
It'll bring very bad luck.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:07.910
I know.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.340
But I don't want to let it go.

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:12.920
The person trapped inside of it

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:16.400
is the most important person in my life.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.420
Tsugumi?

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:32.440
Who turned my lovely 
Tsugumi into a thief?

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.440
Dolly!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.250
I finally found it.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.660
Give me that which holds

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.450
the soul of my beloved king, 
the black camellia.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.950
I don't have it!

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:47.830
What?

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.280
My Hayate is trapped inside of here, now.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.960
Your beloved died some 13 years ago.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.590
He died when the body of my 
father here, Shin Hayek, died.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:02.340
What are you talking about?

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.990
I stabbed myself with the

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.810
black camellia on my way to see you.

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.190
Then I had an accident.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:15.540
Your king died when my body died.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:20.280
Your duty is finished.

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:23.780
Dolly, give back

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.780
the ring that your crow took from me.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.660
The ring signifies our eternal love.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.040
Lies. It's all lies. All lies!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.310
Lies, lies, lies!

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:39.670
If I stab someone with 
the black camellia,

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:41.980
my beloved should appear again.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:44.930
I should be reunited with my beloved!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.930
You can never be reunited with 
someone who's dead.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:53.110
You're lying!

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:55.190
Give me back the black camellia.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:56.780
I won't!

00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:00.230
There's someone very 
important to me inside it.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.030
My beloved Hayate!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:05.160
Then I will take it by force!

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.880
Without the element of surprise, 
you can't beat me!

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:24.090
I'm sure you realize the 
police have been notified.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:25.700
That said...

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.630
Give me back my money!

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:30.340
There!

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:31.930
Maria-san?

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:32.670
Shit!

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.050
Didn't plan on using the hostage for our runaway now.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.070
You take my money, 
and now you take my friend hostage.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.910
Could you people be any more rotten?!

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:43.760
<i>Freeze! I'll shoot!</i>

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:47.070
<i>I'm sorry! I've made a mess of things!</i>

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.830
Oh, it's not your fault, Maria-san.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.320
<i>It seems I made a mistake.</i>

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:51.820
<i>Shut up</i>

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:53.280
<i>when I'm talking!</i>

00:21:57.410 --> 00:22:01.060
Whoa! What the hell?!

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.350
Give me back my black camellia!

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:08.770
Give me back my beloved!
